  "headline": "13 Dead and 14 Trapped in Illegal Pongkor Gold Mine Landslide",
  "seoTitle": "Illegal Gold Mine Collapse in Pongkor Bogor",
  "metaDescription": "A landslide at an illegal gold mine in Pongkor, Bogor has left 13 people dead and 14 others trapped, with search and rescue operations currently underway.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "A landslide at an illegal gold mining site in Pongkor, Bogor, has resulted in 13 confirmed deaths.",
    "Search and rescue operations are ongoing for 14 individuals who remain trapped in the mine shafts.",
    "Authorities have also recently raided an illegal gold processing facility operating under the guise of a cattle farm in the region."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A fatal landslide has occurred at an unauthorized gold mining site located in the Pongkor region of Bogor, Indonesia. Following the incident, rescue teams from Basarnas are conducting observations of multiple mine shafts to assess safety conditions before proceeding with extraction efforts. Officials have confirmed that 13 victims have been recovered and identified, while another 14 people are currently missing and presumed trapped within the underground network. Parallel to the search operations, the Bareskrim Polri has conducted enforcement actions against illegal gold processing activities in the vicinity of Mount Salak. Investigations revealed a facility masquerading as a cattle farm that had reportedly been operational since 2023, generating approximately 1.4 billion rupiah from illegal activities. These operations have been linked to the broader issue of unregulated mining practices within the Mount Halimun Salak National Park region.",
